# Select Target Computer
#
# Please copy this file to Makefile.systype and uncomment your
# system. Don't commit changes to this file unless you add support for
# a new system.
#
#############

#SYSTYPE="github-ubuntu"
#SYSTYPE="Frontera"
#SYSTYPE="MacBookCellar"
#SYSTYPE="Expanse"
#SYSTYPE="CaltechHPC"
#SYSTYPE="RUSTY"
# Rusty, per-architecture (explicit -march, so you can build off-target).
# See the RUSTY_* blocks in the Makefile for run recipes; the short version:
#   pure MPI one rank per core; hybrid costs throughput; if you build with
#   OPENMP you MUST add --cpu-bind=cores to srun or ranks silently stack onto
#   the same cores; scale MaxMemSize with ranks-per-node.
#SYSTYPE="RUSTY_GENOA"     # 96 cores/node, 1.5 TB, --constraint=genoa        <- fastest
#SYSTYPE="RUSTY_ROME"      # 128 cores/node, 1.0 TB, --constraint=rome
#SYSTYPE="RUSTY_ICELAKE"   # 64 cores/node, 1.0 TB, --constraint='icelake&cpu'
